WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.660
Local inference can reduce dependence on external model services,

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:05.000
but privacy still requires design.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.130
Data boundaries include more than the prompt box.

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:12.000
Files, attachments, chat histories, local logs, screenshots, exports, backups,

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.000
shared folders, and connected tools can all carry information from the workflow.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.190
Before a workflow is repeated, classify the data.

00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:22.490
Public information, internal notes, project-confidential material, personal data,

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:23.780
customer data, regulated data,

00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:26.995
and sensitive operational details may require different handling.

00:00:26.995 --> 00:00:29.000
Some data may be fine for a local session.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.995
Other data may need redaction, approval, or a different workflow entirely.

00:00:32.995 --> 00:00:35.975
Do not assume every local workflow is safe for every dataset.

00:00:35.975 --> 00:00:39.995
A model session may be local, but the output may be copied into email, documents,

00:00:39.995 --> 00:00:41.000
source control, tickets, or chat.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.995
Backups may sync files. Logs may preserve prompts or response fragments.

00:00:44.995 --> 00:00:48.995
A useful boundary follows the data after the model response is generated.

00:00:48.995 --> 00:00:52.475
Retention choices matter. Decide which prompts, outputs, settings,

00:00:52.475 --> 00:00:53.945
and exported files should be kept.

00:00:53.945 --> 00:00:56.000
Remove temporary material when it is no longer useful.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:59.995
Keep important records only where they belong and where access is appropriate.

00:00:59.995 --> 00:01:01.971
Privacy is both technical and behavioral.

00:01:01.971 --> 00:01:06.190
Device security, file permissions, workspace separation, redaction habits,

00:01:06.190 --> 00:01:08.975
cautious sharing, and clear review rules all support sovereign AI.

00:01:08.975 --> 00:01:12.995
The safest local workflow is explicit about what data enters, what leaves,

00:01:12.995 --> 00:01:13.945
and what remains stored.

00:01:13.945 --> 00:01:17.990
When the boundary is unclear, pause and decide before adding more files or automation.
